1
00:00:27,260 --> 00:00:30,220
Be careful. He's strong.

2
00:00:30,700 --> 00:00:31,600
Got it.

3
00:00:33,350 --> 00:00:37,090
Wh-What's going on? It's still so early.

4
00:00:41,830 --> 00:00:45,070
He doesn't seem to be here.

5
00:00:45,470 --> 00:00:47,950
There's so much crap, it's hard to tell.

6
00:00:49,100 --> 00:00:50,960
Throw it all out.

7
00:00:54,430 --> 00:00:57,230
What the hell are they doing?

8
00:00:59,390 --> 00:01:00,490
He escaped.

9
00:01:01,330 --> 00:01:02,030
What?

10
00:01:02,530 --> 00:01:04,050
Gardar escaped.

11
00:01:04,600 --> 00:01:08,300
What other reason would
they have to search our shed?

12
00:01:14,760 --> 00:01:15,990
Arnheid!

13
00:03:09,420 --> 00:03:13,710
Great Purpose

14
00:03:18,490 --> 00:03:20,010
Wait, Einar!

15
00:03:20,890 --> 00:03:24,390
Stop, Einar!

16
00:03:25,200 --> 00:03:29,500
If Gardar escaped,
he'll look for Arnheid again.

17
00:03:31,980 --> 00:03:34,250
What will you accomplish by going to Arnheid?

18
00:03:34,950 --> 00:03:37,020
Will you drive back Gardar?

19
00:03:40,520 --> 00:03:43,600
I don't know, but...

20
00:03:45,400 --> 00:03:51,260
There must be something I can do for Arnheid.

21
00:04:14,430 --> 00:04:15,760
Arnheid!

22
00:04:21,850 --> 00:04:23,620
It's not him.

23
00:04:23,620 --> 00:04:27,050
It's not Gardar. Just two slaves.

24
00:04:28,310 --> 00:04:31,620
What are their names again?

25
00:04:31,620 --> 00:04:34,130
You mean the master's slaves.

26
00:04:35,260 --> 00:04:37,600
Thorfinn and Einar, huh?

27
00:04:38,010 --> 00:04:40,100
Yeah, those guys.

28
00:04:40,100 --> 00:04:42,110
What are they doing here?

29
00:04:43,460 --> 00:04:46,390
What should we do, boss?
Should we chase them off?

30
00:04:48,330 --> 00:04:52,860
No, leave them alone.
Let them do what they want.

31
00:05:05,400 --> 00:05:08,650
Um, Arnheid...

32
00:05:11,270 --> 00:05:15,410
Yes. You're here about Gardar.

33
00:05:17,100 --> 00:05:18,800
You know?

34
00:05:22,620 --> 00:05:23,410
Yes.

35
00:05:26,110 --> 00:05:29,820
I helped him escape.

36
00:05:31,400 --> 00:05:34,830
I cut the ropes binding him.

37
00:05:38,840 --> 00:05:42,530
Gardar, he... the man watching him....

38
00:05:43,030 --> 00:05:51,570
I thought we'd both be killed, so I...

39
00:06:00,010 --> 00:06:10,010
Then Gardar killed all the other guests
who came to see what was happening.

40
00:06:16,940 --> 00:06:18,570
More dead guests...

41
00:06:19,090 --> 00:06:21,770
The situation couldn't be worse.

42
00:06:27,130 --> 00:06:28,050
Einar...

43
00:06:28,990 --> 00:06:31,090
We're being watched by guests.

44
00:06:31,090 --> 00:06:34,970
Kneel next to Arnheid and
pretend to wash dishes.

45
00:06:42,360 --> 00:06:46,410
Stay calm, and tell us what's happening.

46
00:06:49,960 --> 00:06:55,500
Gardar was badly injured in the f-fight.

47
00:06:56,840 --> 00:07:03,790
We fled here in the rain,
to the old master's house.

48
00:07:05,530 --> 00:07:11,530
But Gardar lost consciousness
while I was tending his wounds.

49
00:07:12,600 --> 00:07:15,120
He was too heavy to carry.

50
00:07:15,750 --> 00:07:20,050
I was barely able to hide him.

51
00:07:21,630 --> 00:07:24,400
So Gardar is here.

52
00:07:24,990 --> 00:07:30,430
Yes. The old master helped me.

53
00:07:31,030 --> 00:07:34,720
Snake and his men arrived soon after.

54
00:07:36,330 --> 00:07:43,500
They seem to think Gardar fled
and is hiding somewhere.

55
00:07:45,350 --> 00:07:51,210
They're waiting for Gardar
to come for me at the house.

56
00:07:51,640 --> 00:07:54,970
Mister Snake and two other men are inside.

57
00:07:58,120 --> 00:08:02,710
Why... Why would you do something
so reckless by yourself?

58
00:08:03,400 --> 00:08:07,730
And after you said we'd wait out the storm
for the sake of the child inside you.

59
00:08:15,630 --> 00:08:17,930
Why?

60
00:08:27,710 --> 00:08:29,120
Perhaps...

61
00:08:30,680 --> 00:08:35,020
Perhaps I was dreaming.

62
00:08:35,910 --> 00:08:42,650
Dreaming of a life as part of a family
with Gardar and the child inside me.

63
00:08:44,380 --> 00:08:49,470
I thought that perhaps he had returned...

64
00:08:53,030 --> 00:08:57,170
I thought he'd returned.

65
00:09:02,840 --> 00:09:11,040
Those eyes that used to be
so full of confidence...

66
00:09:17,080 --> 00:09:19,870
They looked so miserable.

67
00:09:22,680 --> 00:09:30,290
We've lived so miserably
since we lost Hjalti.

68
00:09:33,550 --> 00:09:37,970
But I still dream...

69
00:09:50,990 --> 00:09:55,450
How are Gardar's injuries?
Has the bleeding stopped?

70
00:10:00,710 --> 00:10:05,120
He was bleeding badly
from the right side of his chest.

71
00:10:06,190 --> 00:10:10,700
He was still bleeding when I hid him.

72
00:10:13,080 --> 00:10:15,210
Every moment counts.

73
00:10:23,910 --> 00:10:25,130
Arnheid...

74
00:10:27,080 --> 00:10:32,320
Are you prepared to cast your lot with Gardar?

75
00:10:42,090 --> 00:10:47,370
If you want to live with Gardar,
then you'll have to flee together.

76
00:10:49,640 --> 00:10:51,900
But you're pregnant.

77
00:10:52,680 --> 00:10:55,180
The road ahead will be difficult.

78
00:10:56,940 --> 00:10:59,040
But if you still want to try,

79
00:11:00,650 --> 00:11:02,590
then I will help you.

80
00:11:04,570 --> 00:11:07,930
It's the only option left.

81
00:11:18,330 --> 00:11:22,080
The only option, huh?

82
00:11:26,120 --> 00:11:28,850
I'll help, too.

83
00:11:28,850 --> 00:11:32,160
Together, we may be able to do something.

84
00:11:33,630 --> 00:11:34,780
Thorfinn...

85
00:11:52,770 --> 00:11:54,780
Ow! What—

86
00:11:55,120 --> 00:11:56,470
Don't sleep.

87
00:11:56,470 --> 00:12:00,450
If you take your eyes off Arnheid again,
I'll break your nose.

88
00:12:00,910 --> 00:12:03,580
Y-Yes, boss. Sorry.

89
00:12:08,650 --> 00:12:09,520
Who's there?

90
00:12:11,790 --> 00:12:15,740
I'd like to begin preparing lunch.

91
00:12:18,920 --> 00:12:21,700
Take the tools you need and cook in the yard.

92
00:12:21,700 --> 00:12:25,570
You're the bait.
Stay where you'll be seen.

93
00:12:27,660 --> 00:12:30,370
Very well. I understand.

94
00:12:41,350 --> 00:12:44,910
What a pitiful bunch.

95
00:12:45,740 --> 00:12:47,820
Right, Snake?

96
00:12:51,150 --> 00:12:58,690
They say inferior people
can't help but become slaves.

97
00:12:59,450 --> 00:13:01,900
That it's where they belong.

98
00:13:03,070 --> 00:13:06,270
But I don't think so.

99
00:13:06,720 --> 00:13:12,220
Slaves were just unlucky. That's all.

100
00:13:13,190 --> 00:13:19,310
If you and I had been unlucky,
we might've ended up as slaves, too.

101
00:13:20,350 --> 00:13:24,570
So what? That's got nothing to do with this.

102
00:13:24,990 --> 00:13:27,340
He killed five of my men.

103
00:13:27,690 --> 00:13:30,540
I won't be satisfied until he's dead.

104
00:13:32,090 --> 00:13:35,400
I can't walk around wearing this sword

105
00:13:35,400 --> 00:13:38,510
when I'm crying myself to sleep
over my unavenged men.

106
00:13:43,150 --> 00:13:46,340
Then throw away your sword.

107
00:13:50,910 --> 00:13:56,860
Even I can tell that sword
isn't from around here.

108
00:13:57,320 --> 00:14:01,970
There was a reason you ended up here.

109
00:14:03,000 --> 00:14:09,180
But I doubt throwing away your sword
would allow you to escape whatever it was.

110
00:14:10,920 --> 00:14:15,650
Enough talking, Gramps.
It's time for your nap.

111
00:14:18,470 --> 00:14:21,390
You can have my farm.

112
00:14:22,310 --> 00:14:26,870
Work the land. Produce life.

113
00:14:26,870 --> 00:14:30,510
That's better than swinging around a sword.

114
00:14:34,110 --> 00:14:40,650
I can no longer stand and walk.
Soon I will die.

115
00:14:41,350 --> 00:14:45,310
It's a good opportunity for you
to straighten out your life.

116
00:14:47,900 --> 00:14:53,390
I owe you for reading the Bible to me.

117
00:14:57,050 --> 00:15:00,770
Don't talk about that nonsense now.

118
00:15:00,770 --> 00:15:02,770
I'm not doing no stinking field work.

119
00:15:04,760 --> 00:15:05,760
Boss.

120
00:15:05,760 --> 00:15:06,490
Huh?

121
00:15:06,840 --> 00:15:08,720
There's someone out there.

122
00:15:12,200 --> 00:15:15,350
Over there. Third tree from the back.

123
00:15:16,430 --> 00:15:19,480
That's probably him in its shadow.

124
00:15:23,020 --> 00:15:24,530
All right.

125
00:15:56,730 --> 00:15:57,770
They're coming out.

126
00:15:58,230 --> 00:16:01,290
One, two, three...

127
00:16:01,770 --> 00:16:03,480
That's all of them.

128
00:16:07,990 --> 00:16:10,560
I'm counting on you, Einar.

129
00:16:28,130 --> 00:16:29,620
Spread out.

130
00:16:30,050 --> 00:16:32,890
We'll follow him from different
positions and vantages.

131
00:16:37,950 --> 00:16:42,770
Sir, I'm sorry, but I need to
borrow your horse and cart.

132
00:16:42,770 --> 00:16:46,430
I promise I'll pay you back
by working for you.

133
00:16:47,350 --> 00:16:49,810
Don't worry about that.

134
00:16:49,810 --> 00:16:53,190
More importantly, load me into the cart.

135
00:16:53,190 --> 00:16:58,160
If I'm there, we'll be able to travel
around the farm unquestioned.

136
00:16:58,160 --> 00:17:02,570
But we can't involve you in this...

137
00:17:03,720 --> 00:17:06,420
I'm already involved.

138
00:17:06,910 --> 00:17:10,670
Now quit arguing and help me.

139
00:17:11,580 --> 00:17:14,960
Y-Yes, sir. Thank you.

140
00:17:19,930 --> 00:17:21,410
Damn that Gardar...

141
00:17:21,810 --> 00:17:23,710
He's trying to flee into the woods.

142
00:17:24,310 --> 00:17:27,450
We won't be able to use
the horses in the woods.

143
00:17:27,450 --> 00:17:29,900
Catch him. Don't let him enter the woods.

144
00:17:33,990 --> 00:17:36,330
Damn it! It's so far away...

145
00:17:53,630 --> 00:17:56,770
He's alive. His wounds were treated well.

146
00:17:58,040 --> 00:18:00,700
But he's as cold as a stone.

147
00:18:01,670 --> 00:18:03,490
He lost too much blood.

148
00:18:05,000 --> 00:18:07,470
Please hang in there.

149
00:18:12,750 --> 00:18:13,990
He's fast.

150
00:18:14,650 --> 00:18:18,850
A gravely injured man
could never run that fast.

151
00:18:20,360 --> 00:18:22,580
Spider! Badger!

152
00:18:22,580 --> 00:18:24,480
Stay on him.

153
00:18:25,000 --> 00:18:27,110
Don't force a confrontation.

154
00:18:27,110 --> 00:18:31,340
If that's Gardar, you won't
stand a chance against him.

155
00:18:31,950 --> 00:18:34,070
I'll send reinforcements later.

156
00:18:34,070 --> 00:18:36,190
Keep following him until then.

157
00:18:36,630 --> 00:18:38,090
You got that?

158
00:18:38,430 --> 00:18:39,710
I'm counting on you guys.

159
00:18:40,600 --> 00:18:43,600
What? Wait, where are you going, boss?

160
00:18:46,920 --> 00:18:49,090
The cart is ready.

161
00:18:49,090 --> 00:18:51,360
We'll hurry toward the border to the south.

162
00:18:51,860 --> 00:18:55,910
Once you're out of the country, it'll be
difficult for the guests to pursue you.

163
00:18:56,630 --> 00:18:59,110
I'll leave you partway to distract them.

164
00:18:59,110 --> 00:19:01,260
I'll draw as many pursuers to me as I can.

165
00:19:02,840 --> 00:19:06,960
Sir, could you accompany them
to the edge of the farm?

166
00:19:07,270 --> 00:19:09,760
Got it.

167
00:19:42,010 --> 00:19:44,300
I didn't hear horses.

168
00:19:47,910 --> 00:19:50,300
Did he dismount and run here?

169
00:19:56,230 --> 00:19:57,630
I see.

170
00:19:58,800 --> 00:20:01,810
So he's unconscious.

171
00:20:02,590 --> 00:20:05,580
No wonder I couldn't sense him.

172
00:20:12,360 --> 00:20:13,610
Thorfinn...

173
00:20:25,080 --> 00:20:29,710
Just so you know, Thorfinn,
I'm not here to negotiate.

174
00:20:32,120 --> 00:20:34,610
Hand over Gardar.

175
00:20:35,580 --> 00:20:37,120
Otherwise,

176
00:20:38,350 --> 00:20:39,450
I'll kill you.

177
00:20:46,520 --> 00:20:48,050
There were three pursuers.

178
00:20:48,590 --> 00:20:51,020
But only Snake is here.

179
00:20:51,020 --> 00:20:52,610
I don't sense the others.

180
00:20:53,550 --> 00:20:58,190
If I can subdue him somehow,
we can still escape.

181
00:20:59,610 --> 00:21:03,530
I'll slip past his sword and
deal a single blow to his chin.

182
00:21:06,780 --> 00:21:09,280
You gonna fight him, Thorfinn?

183
00:21:09,280 --> 00:21:12,640
Good grief. I guess
you can't help it this time.

184
00:21:13,040 --> 00:21:15,590
You're helping someone.

185
00:21:15,590 --> 00:21:18,930
You've got a good reason to raise your fists.

186
00:21:21,260 --> 00:21:23,550
But, you know,

187
00:21:23,910 --> 00:21:27,870
I'm sure he's got a good reason, too.

188
00:21:28,930 --> 00:21:31,150
What will you do, Thorfinn?

189
00:21:31,570 --> 00:21:39,200
Will you remain a pacifist, or will you
fight him in order to help someone else?

190
00:21:41,940 --> 00:21:45,840
Which road leads to becoming a true warrior?

191
00:21:46,390 --> 00:21:48,860
There's no time to think about it.

192
00:21:50,450 --> 00:21:53,210
Look. He's right in front of you.

193
00:22:57,400 --> 00:23:00,210
Do you think you can beat him
while you're still half-asleep?

194
00:23:32,350 --> 00:23:34,060
That's an odd stance.

195
00:23:34,790 --> 00:23:36,810
Not right for a spear or an ax...

196
00:23:37,580 --> 00:23:38,540
A sword?

197
00:23:41,600 --> 00:23:42,640
No...

198
00:25:37,050 --> 00:25:39,970
The Road Home

199
00:25:38,280 --> 00:25:39,420
"The Road Home."
